# phonon: fix aligned load on a misaligned accumulator in complex multiplyAccumulate
#
# Steam Audio 4.8.1 (ValveSoftware/steam-audio). Apply to the third_party/steam-audio submodule
# before building phonon (see ../README.md "Steam Audio" build recipe).
#
# THE BUG
# ArrayMath::multiplyAccumulate(int, const complex_t*, const complex_t*, complex_t*) has an aligned
# and an unaligned SSE code path, chosen by float4::isAligned(in1) && isAligned(in2) && isAligned(accum).
# The UNALIGNED path correctly uses loadu/storeu for the inputs and the output store, but reads the
# accumulator with float4::load (the *aligned* movaps/addps form). When that branch is taken precisely
# because `accum` is 16-byte-misaligned, the aligned read access-violates (0xC0000005).
#
# WHEN IT FIRES
# The reflection convolution (OverlapSaveConvolutionEffect) accumulates per ambisonic channel into
# mFFTWet[i], a buffer whose per-channel stride is numSpectrumSamples * sizeof(complex). numSpectrumSamples
# = nextpow2(2*frameSize)/2 + 1 is ALWAYS odd (2^k + 1), so the stride is 8 mod 16 bytes and every ODD
# channel (1, 3, ...) is 16-byte-misaligned. Result: any multichannel (ambisonic order >= 1) reflection
# effect crashes at channel index 1 on the first apply. Order-0 / single-channel (channel 0 only, always
# aligned) is unaffected — which is why it looks intermittent.
#
# THE FIX
# Use float4::loadu for the accumulator read in the unaligned branch (one character: load -> loadu).
# The aligned branch (only entered when accum IS aligned) is left untouched.
#
# Upstream: this is the (still open, root-cause-unknown) ValveSoftware/steam-audio issue #546
# ("Seg Fault when trying to use Reflection Sim with IPL_REFLECTIONEFFECTTYPE_CONVOLUTION" — crashes
# at channel i=1 with 4-channel first-order ambisonics). That report has the symptom but not the
# cause/fix below; worth posting this diagnosis + one-liner there.
# https://github.com/ValveSoftware/steam-audio/issues/546
--- a/core/src/core/array_math.cpp
+++ b/core/src/core/array_math.cpp
@@ -257,7 +257,7 @@ void ArrayMath::multiplyAccumulate(int size,

             auto y = float4::add(float4::mul(b1, x2), float4::mul(b0, float4::mul(b3, b4)));

-            y = float4::add(y, float4::load(&outData[i]));
+            y = float4::add(y, float4::loadu(&outData[i]));   /* loadu: this branch is taken when accum is misaligned */

             float4::storeu(&outData[i], y);
         }
